Procure Data for csv_editing.py from: https://cris.dot.state.tx.us/public/Query/app/query-builder/disclaimer

Procure Data for weather from: https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/search/data-search/global-hourly

In order to run the 'csv_editing.py' script, you will need to get your data.csv and weather.csv (names do not matter)

# # # # # # # # # # # # # # # # # WARNING

This process will take several minutes
Sometimes there will be updates in the console, but these can be infrequent

# # # # # # # # # # # # # # # # # WARNING

1. Remove the query information from the downloaded CSV files. Everything up to the column headers should be removed. The column headers should be the first line of the file.
2. Place the CSV files in the same directory as 'csv_editing.py'
3. Enter the names of your files in csv_weather.py and csv_editing.py

csv_weather.py:
csv_editing.py: Line 506

4. Run csv_weather.py first
5. Run csv_editor.py second
6. Result should be TrainingData.csv
